          %h3#GeneralGaugeBackgroundsAndParameterizedWZWModels General gauge backgrounds and parameterized WZW models
          %p
            The traditional construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            theory of the heterotic string produces via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
            of the left-moving worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            only those
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+fields"} background gauge fields
            which are reducible to
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 16
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(16)/\mathbb{Z}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            (
            %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"}> Distler-Sharpe 10, sections 2-4
            ). But it is known that, for instance, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+F-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between F-theory and heterotic string theory
            produces more general gauge backgrounds (
            %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"}> Distler-Sharpe 10, section 5
            ).
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"}> Distler-Sharpe 10, section 7
            ), following (
            %a{:href => "#GatesSiegel88"}> Gates-Siegel 88
            ), it is argued that the way to fix this is to consider
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+models"} parameterized WZW models
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "-background" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly"} Green-Schwarz anomaly
            (and its cancellation) of the heterotic string now comes out as being equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            (and its lifting) for such a parameterized WZW term to exist.
          %p
            Moreover, where the traditional construction only produces level-1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebras"} current algebras
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"} Distler-Sharpe 10, section 8.5
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            of the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+models"} parameterized WZW models
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+genera"} equivariant elliptic genera
            found by Liu and Ando (
            %a{:href => "#Ando07"}> Ando 07
            ).
          %p
            However, presently questions remain concerning formulating a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            for strings propagating on the total space of the bundle, as it is only the chiral part of the geometric WZW model that appears in the heterotic string. (…)
          %h3#SuperspaceFormulation Superspace formulation
          %p
