                    supergravity theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BonoraSuperGS.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#LechnerTonin08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+Lechner"}> Kurt Lechner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Tonin"} Mario Tonin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superspace formulations of ten-dimensional supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0802.3869"} arXiv:0802.3869
          %h3#in_elliptic_cohomology In elliptic cohomology
          %p
            For more mathematically precise discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            see also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Witten+genus#TwistedWittenGenus"} Witten genus – Heterotic (twisted) Witten genus, loop group representations and parameterized WZW models
          %h3#general_flux_backgrounds_and_parameterized_wzw_models General flux backgrounds and parameterized WZW models
          %p
            Discussion of heterotic strings whoe
            = succeed "-sector" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            originates with
          %ul
            %li#GatesSiegel88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Warren+Siegel"} Warren Siegel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Leftons, Rightons, Nonlinear
                    = succeed "-Models," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/251286/"} spire
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strings, superstrings, and two-dimensional lagrangian field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Functional integration, geometry, and strings
            %li#GKKS91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                , S. Ketov, S. Kozenko, O. Solovev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Lagrangian chiral coset construction of heterotic string theories in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,0)
                    superspace
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/314337/?ln=en"} spire
          %p and is further expanded on in
          %ul
            %li#DistlerSharpe10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"} Eric Sharpe
              = succeed "," do
                %em Heterotic compactifications with principal bundles for general groups and general levels
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0701244"} arXiv:hep-th/0701244
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Sharpe08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"}> Eric Sharpe
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Recent developments in heterotic compactifications
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"} Eric Sharpe
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+Greenspoon"} Arthur Greenspoon
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=AMSIP-44"} Advances in String Theory: The First Sowers Workshop in Theoretical Physics
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.phys.vt.edu/sowers/talks/sharpe-sowers.pdf"} pdf slides (39-49)
          %p
            The relation of this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            is amplified in
          %ul
            %li#Ando07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant elliptic cohomology and the Fibered WZW models of Distler and Sharpe
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ucsb.edu/~drm/GTPseminar/2007-fall.php"} talk 2007
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ucsb.edu/~drm/GTPseminar/notes/20071026-ando/20071026-malmendier.pdf"}> lecture notes pdf
              )
          %h3#on_elliptic_fibrations On elliptic fibrations
          %p
            Compactified on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            or, more generally,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+bundle"} stable bundle
            on the compact space. Dually this is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            compactification on a
            = succeed "-bundles." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
          %p The basis of this story is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Robert Friedman,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              %em Vector Bundles And F-Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701162"}> arXiv:hep-th/9701162
              )
          %p A more formal discussion is in
          %ul
            %li
              B. Andreas and D. Hernandez Ruiperez, Adv. Theor. Math. Phys. Volume 7, Number 5 (2003), 751-786
              %em Comments on N = 1 Heterotic String Vacua
              (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1111510429"}> project Euclid
              )
          %h3#dualities_2 Dualities
          %h4#with_type_i_superstring_theory With type I superstring theory
          %p The original conjecture is due to
          %ul
            %li#Witten05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , section 5 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"} arXiv:hep-th/9503124
          %p More details are then in
          %ul
            %li#PolchinskiWitten96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Evidence for Heterotic - Type I String Duality
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510169"} arXiv:hep-th/9510169
          %h4#DualityWithFTheory
            With
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+F-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between F-theory and heterotic string theory
            originates in
          %ul
            %li#Sen96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                %em F-theory and Orientifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605150"}> arXiv:hep-th/9605150
                )
            %li#FriedmanMorganWitten97
              %p
                Robert Friedman,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                %em Vector Bundles And F Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701162"}> arXiv:hep-th/9701162
                )
          %p Reviews include
          %ul
            %li#Donagi98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ron+Donagi"}> Ron Donagi
                ,
                %em ICMP lecture on heterotic/F-theory duality
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9802093"}> arXiv:hep-th/9802093
                )
            %li
              %p
                Björn Andreas,
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                  Heterotic/F-theory duality
                PhD thesis (
                %a{:href => "http://edoc.hu-berlin.de/dissertationen/physik/andreas-bjoern/PDF/Andreas.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %div
            %h3#FlavorOnSingleHeteroticM5BranesReferences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
              \-flavor symmetry on heterotic M5-branes
            %p
              Emergence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+%28particle+physics%29"} flavor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry"} symmetry
              on single
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+M-theory+on+ADE-orbifolds"} heterotic M-theory on ADE-orbifolds
              (in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%281%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(1,0) SCFT
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+instantons"} small instantons
              in
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Abhijit Gadde, Babak Haghighat,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joonho+Kim"} Joonho Kim
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seok+Kim"} Seok Kim
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em 6d String Chains
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.04614"} arXiv:1504.04614
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP02(2018)143"} doi:10.1007/JHEP02(2018)143
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kantaro+Ohmori"}> Kantaro Ohmori
                  , Section 2.3.1 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Six-Dimensional Superconformal Field Theories and Their Torus Compactifications
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9789811330919"} springer:book/9789811330919
            %p
              Argument for this by translation under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
              to
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half+NS5-brane"} half NS5-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6%2FD8-brane+bound+state"} D6/D8-brane bound state
              systems in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I%27+string+theory"} type I' string theory
            %p Reviewed in:
            %ul
              %li
                Santiago Cabrera,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"} Amihay Hanany
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Magnetic Quivers, Higgs Branches, and 6d
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=(1,0)
                    Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.12293"} arXiv:1904.12293
            %p
              The emergence of flavor in these
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half+NS5-brane"} half NS5-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6%2FD8-brane+bound+state"} D6/D8-brane bound state
              systems, due to the semi-infinite extension of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
              making them act as
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+branes"} flavor branes
            %ul
              %li#HananyZaffaroni98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"}> Amihay Hanany
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Zaffaroni"} Alberto Zaffaroni
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Branes and Six Dimensional Supersymmetric Theories
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9712145"} arXiv:hep-th/9712145
              %li#BrunnerKarch97
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilka+Brunner"}> Ilka Brunner
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Karch"} Andreas Karch
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Branes at Orbifolds versus Hanany Witten in Six Dimensions
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9712143"} arXiv:hep-th/9712143
            %p Reviewed in:
            %ul
              %li#ApruzziFazzi17
                Fabio Apruzzi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Fazzi"} Marco Fazzi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi AdS
                            %mn 7
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi CFT
                            %mn 6
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7/CFT_6
                    with orientifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.03235"} arXiv:1712.03235
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"}> Amihay Hanany
                , Noppadol Mekareeya,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The Small
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                    Instanton and the Kraft Procesi Transition
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.01129"} arXiv:1801.01129
        .revisedby
